                <pb facs="0264" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg168"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3758g: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Forbes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-31T13:00:00-05:00">January 31, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>30. 1. Navy Department has ordered Admiral Taylor, Commander in Chief United
                    States Asiatic Squadron, Manila, to proceed on flagship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Houston</hi> with available destroyers to Shanghai.</p>
                <pb facs="0265" n="169" xml:id="pg169"/>
                <p>2. Department wishes it to be understood that ship movements and American action
                    involve and imply no threat to anyone but are measures of precaution for
                    ensuring safety of American lives and legitimate interests and fulfilling our
                    responsibilities in general at Shanghai and other exposed ports in the Yangtze
                    and elsewhere in China.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
